{{also|verlies}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etym|gml|de}} {{term|verlies||loss|lang=gml}}, cognate with {{etym|nl|-}} {{term|verlies||id.|lang=nl}} and pertaining to German {{term|verlieren||to lose|lang=de}}. Apparently, the original meaning is “place where someone is lost”; possibly a second word (like “place”, “hole”) has been omitted, although no such compound seems to be attested.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/fɛɐ̯ˈliːs/|/fɐˈliːs/|lang=de}}
* {{homophones|lang=de|verließ}}
* {{rhymes|iːs|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n|Verlieses|Verliese|Verlieschen}}

# [[dungeon]] {{gloss|historic prison in a vault}}
#: ''Gefangene Feinde ließ man in '''Verliesen''' unterhalb der Burg verhungern.''
#:: Captured enemies were starved to death in '''dungeons''' below the castle.
# an [[underground]] [[prison]] or place of [[captivity]]
#: ''Der Vergewaltiger hielt sein Opfer in einem eigens gebauten '''Verlies''' im Keller seines Hauses.''
#:: The rapist held his victim in a specially built '''prison''' in the cellar of his house.

